      ":question/math-academy-id": "e-3644",
      ":question/problem": "Find $f'(x)$ if $f(x) = 2 \\csc x.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Here, we just take the constant out of the derivative and use the result for the derivative of $\\csc x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2csc⁡x) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(csc⁡x) \\\\  & =2(-csc⁡xcot⁡x) \\\\  & =-2csc⁡xcot⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
