        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-104316",
        ":question/problem": "Find ${f}^{'}(x)$ if $f(x)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{csc}x.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "We calculate the derivative using the product rule, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{'}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x}\\operatorname{csc}x) \\\\  & ={e}^{x}(\\operatorname{csc}x)+{e}^{x}(-\\operatorname{csc}x\\operatorname{cot}x) \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\operatorname{csc}x(1-\\operatorname{cot}x)\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
