        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-105299",
        ":question/problem": "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ if $f(x)={2}^{x}csc⁡x.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "We calculate the derivative using the product rule, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({2}^{x}csc⁡x) \\\\  & ={2}^{x}ln⁡2(csc⁡x)+{2}^{x}(-csc⁡xcot⁡x) \\\\  & ={2}^{x}csc⁡x(ln⁡2-cot⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$"
